@startuml Sum_Ssfm_RunCrankFaultIndications_Manager
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype ortho

legend top left
    "Sum_Ssfm_RunCrankFaultIndications_Manager"

**Interfaces Legend**
   //II152 //: ERRH_ExecutionStatus
   //II163 //: Sum_Ssfm_ErrhDebouncerExecution (Error Debouncer)
   //ri122 //: SUSD_ERRH_RunCrankInputStuckHighDiagnosticStatus
   //ri123 //: SUSD_ERRH_RunCrankInputStuckLowDiagnosticStatus
   //ri128 //: Dem_CallbackDTCStatusChangedIndication (Runk Crank Fault Indications)
   //CI03  //: Sum_Ssfm_Errh_C_DTCProcess_RC<n> (High/Low)   
   //pi136 //: DiagnosticMonitor (Dem_SetEventStatus)
   //pi138 //: RunCrankInputStuckHigh_FA_StatusRequest
   //pi139 //: RunCrankInputStuckLow_FA_StatusRequest
   //II184 //: Sum_Ssfm_Errh_GetDTCsDisabled (Sum_Ssfm_DTCsDisabled)   
endlegend

component [SSFM::Sum_Ssfm_RunCrankFaultIndications_Manager] as EC{
	portin ri122
	portin ri123
   portin ri128
	portout pi136
	portout pi138
	portout pi139
	[Sum_Ssfm_RunCrankFaultIndications_Manager]  as E
}

note top of EC
It checks the RunCrankInputStuckHighDiagnosticStatus and 
RunCrankInputStuckLowDiagnosticStatus (from SUSD)
and requests the DEM to set/clear the corresponding DTC. 
After receiving DTC confirmation from DEM via callback function 
Dem_CallbackDTCStatusChangedIndication, it notifies back the SUSD through 
the RunCrankInputStuckHigh_FA_StatusRequest
and RunCrankInputStuckLow_FA_StatusRequest interfaces.
end note

   interface II152
   interface CI03
   interface II163
   interface II184


  II152 -> E
  II163 -> E
  ri122 -> E
  ri123 -> E
  ri128 -> E
  CI03 -> E
  II184 -> E
  E -> pi136
  E -> pi138
  E -> pi139  
@enduml
